{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/verbs.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:33:36.354435Z","id":"4696fa18e5f51b8fede6593db0d03e42df9a857d3b2108898fa31dd4b3dffcc8","body":{"detail":"ClaxVerbs.of reads the last pointer kind from the nearest ClaxPointerScope; apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart does not build one yet. Wrapping MaterialApp (or its builder's child) in ClaxPointerScope makes a mouse or trackpad event switch every ClaxVerbs reader to Click.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"85b4a5f297303029973f7b951fe1243d0b0463e583692391da452c760310a0b2"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the app's root in ClaxPointerScope when the Tap strings move to ClaxVerbs (comment_bar.dart, app.dart, build_notices.dart).","summary":"No ClaxPointerScope is at the app's root yet, so ClaxVerbs.of answers by platform only (Click on macOS, Tap elsewhere), even on a Chromebook with a mouse","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/button.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:33:36.354481Z","id":"d855a9b2d95ac3239b1377460ddb43d049ea124525db25619c100a39da5af210","body":{"detail":"AppKit's default button answers Return anywhere in its window or sheet. ClaxButton cannot do that alone: a Shortcuts widget around the button fires only while focus is inside the button. The surface (ClaxSheet, ClaxDialog) has to bind Return (SingleActivator(LogicalKeyboardKey.enter)) to its default action.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"d2489627d4e0f6a30979717a73572d9e39ac4dfe64075948ecf702954f267f89"},"suggested_fix":"Bind Return to the default action in ClaxSheet and ClaxDialog, with a test that Return presses an isDefault button with focus in a field.","summary":"isDefault only changes how an Apple ClaxButton looks; Return does not press it until the sheet or dialog holding it binds Return","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.980500Z","id":"91f27b9cd18585af391cffbac0c739616430b09f4f0f06a0403127da8d3c326c","body":{"detail":"Autofocus requests are applied in mount order and a later one is discarded once the scope has a focused child (Flutter focus_manager.dart _Autofocus.applyIfValid, scope.focusedChild == null). Focus(autofocus: true) wraps the sheet content, so a ClaxTextField(autofocus: true) in it is ignored and typing goes nowhere until the person clicks the field. The same wrapper in ClaxDialog's _Keys (lib/ui/kit/dialog.dart:131-137) does this to any focusable content of a dialog with a defaultIndex. Escape and Return bindings work from a focused descendant too, so the Focus need not autofocus.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"6dd7df15de648107fe21a0e725a5b709f131aa6b38f1bf0d884335c79b4190ff"},"suggested_fix":"Drop autofocus on the wrapper and let the route's FocusScope or the content take focus; test a sheet with an autofocus field.","summary":"The Apple sheet's own autofocused Focus takes the route's first focus, so a field inside the sheet with autofocus: true never gets focus","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/dialog.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.980742Z","id":"06fd96c6f7bc498b8e9da942519559ed66db3af424d1d18099397b73891d2e18","body":{"detail":"_Keys binds Enter at the dialog root, so on Android or a Chromebook with a keyboard, Tab to Cancel then Enter answers the default, not Cancel (Material buttons activate on Enter). The assert at dialog.dart:44-48 vanishes in release, so a call site that passes a destructive defaultIndex ships a dialog where Return deletes. On the Apple family Return-for-default is the platform rule; on the Material family it is not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"5fc3a03fad273c2439c0882589bdea47722b987fdcfae1a7b01f2e24aca3dd1a"},"suggested_fix":"Bind Return to the default only in the Apple family (or only when no button has focus), and refuse a destructive default in release (drop defaultIndex, or throw).","summary":"Return presses the default action whatever has focus, and the rule that a destructive action is never the default is a debug assert only","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.980782Z","id":"5a8954d2133566089329a5e63960bd3517da38d37cd262713cf1e7e47cf15071","body":{"detail":"showModalBottomSheet(useSafeArea: true) wraps the sheet in SafeArea(bottom: false) (Flutter bottom_sheet.dart:1168), and _SheetBody pads the bottom by 24 + viewInsets.bottom only, not by MediaQuery.viewPaddingOf(context).bottom. The app targets SDK 36 (apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel:297), which is edge to edge on Android 15 and later, so with three-button navigation Cancel and the default button overlap the bar. The phone render (target/flutter-app/shots/kit-surfaces-sheet-phone-light.png) uses a 16 dp gesture bar, where it fits.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":116},"end":{"line":123},"content_hash":"36735f5f5b30ccddfd5a2b5949af8ea2f26fc49badb02711097a2e847b8ab9e3"},"suggested_fix":"Add the bottom view padding (max with the keyboard inset) to the sheet body's bottom padding; render with a 48 dp bottom bar.","summary":"At compact width the sheet's actions sit 24 dp above the screen's bottom edge, under a 48 dp three-button navigation bar","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/toggles.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.980958Z","id":"da8fa250fdf97b8fed353a94d660ba955d8260e7d76744f6482a37fd483a31a5","body":{"detail":"Material: the row's InkWell and the Switch, Checkbox or Radio inside it (only semantics are excluded) are both focusable, so Tab stops twice on each row. Apple: the row is a GestureDetector and the mark a plain Container (toggles.dart:85-93, 146-161, 284-317), so ClaxCheckbox and ClaxRadio cannot be reached or toggled from the keyboard at all, while the Apple ClaxSwitch's CupertinoSwitch can.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":253},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"1363322e450b981a4f04e97c8d59446b91cf5a0bfc63463353dcabecab447763"},"suggested_fix":"Make the row the one focus target (FocusableActionDetector or InkWell with canRequestFocus false on the inner control), Space toggling, with a focus ring in the Apple family.","summary":"Keyboard focus on toggle rows: two tab stops per Material row, none on Apple checkboxes and radios","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/scaffold.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.981287Z","id":"00e17c59ba3636bbe914d01613137de2f82174c7fd5eb297d7dd016aa53ac79e","body":{"detail":"toolbarCarriesTitle is true whenever the family is apple and hasDesktopWindowChrome, but the toolbar that would show title and actions is plan Task 44 (phase 6). A screen moved onto ClaxScaffold before then has no title, no back button and no actions on the Mac. No screen uses ClaxScaffold yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"7e335b7fd7ca7d372dc35b8917edc5d5996a1c344722e53c6c1d2176d6d5ea84"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the AppBar on macOS until a toolbar is installed (a flag Task 44 flips), or move screens onto ClaxScaffold only after Task 44.","summary":"On macOS ClaxScaffold drops its title, leading (Back) and actions, and nothing carries them until the NSToolbar exists","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/toast.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.981456Z","id":"149c4baeaec29311873e9dcd8384cdfda10e516f1716b6de7c1c1223f541a02f","body":{"detail":"SnackBar keeps a toast with an action on screen while MediaQuery.accessibleNavigation is on, and is a liveRegion; the top and inline toasts (toast.dart:205-307) are plain overlay entries dismissed by clock.delay(4 s) unconditionally, with no Semantics(liveRegion: true). A screen-reader user cannot reach Undo or View in time and hears nothing when the toast appears. On the Mac every toast is the inline one (toast.dart:49-52).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"ae181610a781c8afaa1a13174eadbc9eaabe7f590b7690d96533cc99d64419e2"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the card or bar in Semantics(liveRegion: true, container: true) and skip the timed dismissal when accessibleNavigation is on and an action is given.","summary":"The overlay toasts (top, inline) leave after 4 s even with an action and under TalkBack or VoiceOver, and are not announced","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/button.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.981616Z","id":"233bb1f72fdf10705fc3d14da43afc79c1f6760f8be022942a36fc9e3cc93ea2","body":{"detail":"fixedSize Size.fromHeight(24) holds the height whatever the label: 13 pt body at TextScaler.linear(2) needs about 34 pt. macOS has no system text scale today, but the Apple family is iOS's starting point (Dynamic Type) and the review focus asks for text at 200%. No kit render is made at -130 or -200.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"b272a5903823d561ccf323559483251476738c8828314cce1fd91be0c8692c70"},"suggested_fix":"Use minimumSize for 24 pt and let the height grow with the scaled label; add 130%/200% kit-controls renders.","summary":"The Apple ClaxButton is a fixed 24 pt high, so its label clips at large text scales","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/button.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.982781Z","id":"da15489ae41726e3e80c5c69cda167857852929480d70cd18d532d6802cfe17c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d855a9b2d95ac3239b1377460ddb43d049ea124525db25619c100a39da5af210","summary":"ClaxSheet binds no Return either: its actions are caller widgets (lib/ui/kit/sheet.dart:29-97, _SheetBody and _AppleSheet bind only Escape), so a default ClaxButton in an Apple sheet is still pressed only by click. ClaxDialog binds Return (dialog.dart:120-138).","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
